id: regexp/syntax/s5-named-references/0001
area: regexp
op: RegExpInitialize
in: str:"\\k<b>(?<a>x)" str:"u"
out: error: SyntaxError
class: normative
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexpinitialize spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-parsepattern spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-patterns-static-semantics-early-errors spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-groupspecifiersthatmatch ref:regexpref@1
script: new RegExp("\\k<b>(?<a>x)", "u") instanceof RegExp
note: correspondence row S5: AtomEscape :: k GroupName, GroupSpecifiersThatMatch, and \k in a class, which no production gives [NamedCaptureGroups] (B.1.2's ClassEscape reads ~NamedCaptureGroups, so SourceCharacterIdentityEscape admits k; the main grammar's IdentityEscape refuses it); /u: refused (early:undefined-group-name)
since: 31

