note: correspondence row S5: AtomEscape :: k GroupName, GroupSpecifiersThatMatch, and \k in a class, which no production gives [NamedCaptureGroups] (B.1.2's ClassEscape reads ~NamedCaptureGroups, so SourceCharacterIdentityEscape admits k; the main grammar's IdentityEscape refuses it); /: accepted; the outcome holds with B.1.2 alone (without Annex B: error: SyntaxError); Annex B is required of a web-browser host and optional for any other; both engines answer B.1.2's patterns (Broiler.VM's JSD-0081, requirement R5, Annex B syntax where the specification allows it, and bundle sjl-11-001's correspondence, rows S4 and S7, same in both), so each engine's expectation is B.1.2's outcome
