id: regexp/syntax/s7-grammar-and-annex-b/0024
area: regexp
op: RegExpInitialize
in: str:"^*" str:""
out: error: SyntaxError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row S7 (as widened 2026-11-01, owner's decision D-widen): without u, a quantified look-behind, (?<=a)*, (?<=a)?, (?<!a)*, (?<!a){1}, (?<!a){2}, (?<=a){1,2}, and a quantified ^, $ or \b, ^*, $+, \b*, by the constructor and by a literal never evaluated; Broiler.JS answers accepted: the library's parse refuses each and the refusal is caught (BuiltIns/RegExp/JSRegExp.Broiler.cs), and .NET's Regex accepts the translation; the literal's check is the same new Regex; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0081); answered by SJL-11.5, Broiler.JS's cut-over to Broiler.Regex
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexpinitialize spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-parsepattern spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-patterns ref:regexpref@1
script: new RegExp("^*", "") instanceof RegExp
note: correspondence row S7: the main grammar under u, B.1.2's without it: quantified assertions, braces, brackets, class ranges with escapes; /: refused (grammar:nothing-to-repeat)
since: 31

