area: regexp
op: RegExpInitialize
in: str:"a{,5}" str:""
out: value: bool:true
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: bool:true
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: bool:true
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexpinitialize spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-parsepattern spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-patterns spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-parsepattern-annexb spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regular-expressions-patterns ref:regexpref@1
script: new RegExp("a{,5}", "") instanceof RegExp
note: correspondence row S7: the main grammar under u, B.1.2's without it: quantified assertions, braces, brackets, class ranges with escapes; /: accepted; the outcome holds with B.1.2 alone (without Annex B: error: SyntaxError); Annex B is required of a web-browser host and optional for any other; both engines answer B.1.2's patterns (Broiler.VM's JSD-0081, requirement R5, Annex B syntax where the specification allows it, and bundle sjl-11-001's correspondence, rows S4 and S7, same in both), so each engine's expectation is B.1.2's outcome
since: 31

